              "type": "response_end",
              "response": {
                "text": "Alberto builds agents with a strong focus on evaluation, control and cost:\n\n- **Offline evals before shipping:** Agent eval cases are recorded against a real model and replayed in CI with no model or network. A stale recording or an off-topic leak fails the build.\n- **Human in the loop, graded autonomy:** His fraud detection agent recommends approve, reject or request-info, and a human admin decides. It auto-approves only on evidence verified in code, and web sources can hold a decision back but never approve it.\n- **Measured changes:** Every eval run is logged to a history, so changes to prompts, tools or content show up against the previous run.\n- **Cost and limits:** He tracks token budgets per request, per-IP rate limits and a monthly spend cap. Eval reports show mean tokens, latency and cost per case.\n\nStack includes TypeScript, Claude, MCP, PostgreSQL and GCP. For example, the fraud detection agent went from 54% to 8% approved fraud over twelve offline iterations, and it's now set to use Claude Haiku 5.5 at about $0.002 per review. Want details on any of these projects?",
